# accountsservice -- the user account daemon.
#
# It is what gdm reads to draw the list of users on the login screen, what
# gnome-control-center's Users panel writes through, and where a user's icon,
# language and login history live. gnome-initial-setup creates the first account
# through it. A desktop without it has a login screen with no users on it.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://www.freedesktop.org/software/accountsservice/accountsservice-23.13.9.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=adda4cdeae24fa0992e7df3ffff9effa7090be3ac233a3edfdf69d5a9c9b924f
SRC_DIR=accountsservice-23.13.9

# ==============================================================================
# THE LOGIND INTERFACE
# ==============================================================================
# -Delogind=true, and unlike polkit's session_tracking this one is a BOOLEAN
# WHOSE DEFAULT IS false. meson.build:
#
#     if get_option('elogind')
#       logind_dep = dependency('libelogind', version: '>= 229.4')
#     else
#       logind_dep = dependency('libsystemd', version: '>= 186')
#     endif
#
# The default branch asks for libsystemd -- which RESOLVES HERE, because
# elogind's post-install.sh installs a libsystemd.pc symlink for the GNOME
# components that only know that name. So leaving this alone would have built,
# linked against elogind through a compatibility symlink, and never said which
# session tracker it was using. It is set so the recipe states the answer.
#
# What the daemon does with it: it watches logind sessions to know who is logged
# in, which is how the Users panel greys out "delete" for an active account and
# how the login-history fields are filled.
#
# ==============================================================================
# -Dsystemdsystemunitdir=no, WHICH IS THE `required: false` TRAP
# ==============================================================================
#     systemd_dep = dependency('systemd', required: false)
#     assert(systemd_dep.found(), 'systemd required but not found, ...')
#
# The `required: false` is cancelled by an assert on the very next line, so
# reading only the dependency() call gives the wrong answer: with the option at
# its default of '', this is a HARD failure, not a soft one. elogind provides
# libelogind.pc and libsystemd.pc but no systemd.pc, so the assert fires. 'no'
# is upstream's spelling for "install no unit", and it also skips the
# accounts-daemon.service that nothing here could start.
#
# ==============================================================================
# THE REST
# ==============================================================================
# -Dadmin_group=wheel. With the default of '' meson probes for
# /etc/debian_version and /etc/sysconfig/network-scripts and falls back to
# wheel, so the answer is right today by autodetection. It is named because this
# group is the definition of "Administrator" in the Users panel and it must be
# the same group polkit's 50-default.rules names as its admin identity --
# duct-filesystem creates exactly one such group, `wheel`, and two components
# disagreeing about it would produce a user who can administer one thing and
# not the other.
#
# -Dvapi=false. UPSTREAM DEFAULT IS TRUE and vapigen comes from vala, which is
# not packaged. This is the one option here that would fail with a missing
# program rather than a missing library.
#
# -Dintrospection=true. Already the default; named because gnome-control-center
# and gdm reach the daemon through AccountsService-1.0, and because the recipe
# check keys the introspection dependencies off this flag.
#
# -Ddocbook=false and -Dgtk_doc=false are already the upstream defaults here;
# both want tools that are not packaged (xmlto, gtk-doc).
#
# -Dminimum_uid stays at 1000, which is what shadow's useradd allocates from,
# and -Dgdmconffile/-Dlightdmconffile stay at their defaults: they are paths
# compiled in for reading a display manager's configuration, and /etc/gdm/
# custom.conf is where gdm will put it.
MESON_ARGS="-Delogind=true -Dsystemdsystemunitdir=no -Dadmin_group=wheel \
-Dvapi=false -Dintrospection=true -Ddocbook=false -Dgtk_doc=false"
